{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Such as there was none like it in Egypt.</b> It did not say אשר לא היה במצרים כמוהו but rather אשר לא היה כמוהו במצרים, and the meaning of the verse is that there was nothing like it in all the world, and not in Egypt, and it added 'in Egypt' to magnify the wonder beyond measure, because rains do not fall in Egypt regularly, nor does hail, and therefore the marvel was all the greater."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:12.389734334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}